  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EEF &quot;Partnership for Better Energy Use&quot;</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EEF &quot;Partnership for Better Energy Use&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">East Europe Foundations projekt &quot;Partnerships for better energy use   in Ukraine&quot;, bidrar till att &#xf6;ka kapaciteten hos lokala               beslutsfattare och f&#xf6;retagare s&#xe5; att de har verktyg att planera,      utv&#xe4;rdera och implementera strategier och projekt som leder till      energieffektivisering i Lviv regionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EEF project, &quot;Partnerships for better energy use in Ukraine&quot;,     will build the capacities of local government and business leaders to plan, evaluate, implement and measure community-driven energy         efficiency strategies and projects. EEF will piloting this initiative in Lviv oblast of Ukraine, and it will seek to attract other funds    from other sources as well.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has one overall impact goal of &quot;Local communities are increasingly able to implement energy-saving projects (through the example of Lviv oblast).&quot;Their are four impact outcomes:1: Local authorities are increasingly able to implement (i.e. plan, manage and evaluate) energy-saving projects.2: Local authorities apply tools for energy-saving planning at the oblast level.3: Oblast stakeholders (government, business and households) are increasingly able to attract investment into energy-saving projects.4: EEF helps local stakeholders implement reforms oriented at sustainable development of their communities.</narrative>
  </description>
